      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town earned its All‑America City title in 2011, the first time Colorado’s largest suburb received the honor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lakewood%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Heritage Lakewood offers a 60‑minute guided tour that walks visitors through a 1930s farmhouse, a 1948 diner, and a 1920s country school.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lakewoodco.gov/City-Hall/Departments/Community-Resources/Arts-and-Culture/Heritage-Lakewood/Historic-Structures-and-Tours",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A pair of white pole tractor sheds from the 1930s, originally part of the Bonfils Estate, still house vintage vehicles today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lakewoodco.gov/City-Hall/Departments/Community-Resources/Arts-and-Culture/Heritage-Lakewood/Historic-Structures-and-Tours",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lakewood’s public library, part of the Jefferson County system, serves the community with historic archives and modern resources.",
